    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "nLUV36lejBkB"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Customer Tenure and Churn\n",
        "\n",
        "Customer tenure represents the length of time a customer has been with the company. In many subscription-based businesses, newer customers are more likely to churn than long-term customers.\n",
        "\n",
        "Analyzing the relationship between tenure and churn helps determine whether customer loyalty increases over time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 496
        },
        "id": "h8oSaR7_ij_k",
        "outputId": "4c258e41-fde8-4e2d-c048-af3a68f18284"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "image/png": "",
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 800x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))\n",
        "\n",
        "sns.histplot(data=df, x=\"tenure\", hue=\"Churn\", bins=30)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.title(\"Customer Tenure Distribution by Churn Status\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Tenure (Months)\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6H-B2yWkjH9A"
      },
      "source": [
        "The visualization suggests that churn is concentrated among customers with **shorter tenure**. Customers who have recently joined the company appear more likely to churn compared to those who have been customers for longer periods.\n",
        "\n",
        "This pattern suggests that retention strategies may be especially important during the early stages of the customer lifecycle."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2539ofn4jiXH"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Contract Type and Churn\n",
        "\n",
        "Customer contract type is another important factor that may influence churn behavior. Customers with shorter or more flexible contracts may find it easier to switch providers compared to customers who are locked into longer-term agreements.\n",
        "\n",
        "Analyzing churn rates across different contract types can reveal whether contract structure plays a role in customer retention."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
