          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))\n",
        "\n",
        "sns.countplot(x=\"Contract\", hue=\"Churn\", data=df)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.title(\"Churn by Contract Type\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Contract Type\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Number of Customers\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "LS6Ja307jqP5"
      },
      "source": [
        "Customers with **month-to-month contracts** appear significantly more likely to churn than customers on one-year or two-year contracts.\n",
        "\n",
        "Longer-term contracts may provide incentives for customers to remain with the company, which helps reduce churn rates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zxRz0zsjkLMX"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Monthly Charges and Churn\n",
        "\n",
        "Pricing may influence customer decisions to remain with or leave a service provider. Customers paying higher monthly charges may be more sensitive to price changes or may perceive that they are not receiving sufficient value for the cost.\n",
        "\n",
        "Examining the distribution of monthly charges for churned and retained customers can help determine whether pricing is associated with churn behavior."
      ]
    },
