      "source": [
        "### Feature Importance Insights\n",
        "\n",
        "The logistic regression coefficients and visualization highlight the variables that most strongly influence churn predictions.\n",
        "\n",
        "Several features appear to increase the likelihood of churn. Customers using **fiber optic internet service** show the strongest positive relationship with churn, suggesting that these customers may have higher expectations for service quality or pricing. Additionally, customers who use **electronic check payment methods** or **paperless billing** also appear more likely to leave the company.\n",
        "\n",
        "Demographic characteristics such as **senior citizen status** are also associated with higher churn risk. In contrast, features such as **having dependents** or using **automatic credit card payments** are associated with lower churn probability.\n",
        "\n",
        "These results reinforce the patterns observed during exploratory data analysis and demonstrate how both **service characteristics and customer demographics** influence customer retention."
      ]
    },
