      "source": [
        "### Model Evaluation\n",
        "\n",
        "The logistic regression model was evaluated using a confusion matrix, classification report, and ROC-AUC score. These metrics help assess the model’s ability to correctly identify customers who churn versus those who remain with the company.\n",
        "\n",
        "The confusion matrix provides insight into how many churned and non-churned customers were correctly classified. The classification report summarizes precision, recall, and F1-score for each class, which are important metrics when evaluating classification performance.\n",
        "\n",
        "The ROC-AUC score measures the model’s ability to distinguish between churned and non-churned customers across different classification thresholds. A higher ROC-AUC value indicates stronger predictive performance."
      ]
