        "The logistic regression model achieved a **ROC-AUC score of approximately 0.83**, indicating strong performance in distinguishing between customers who churn and those who remain with the company.\n",
        "\n",
        "This result suggests that the available features contain meaningful predictive information related to customer churn. Variables such as **tenure, contract type, internet service type, and monthly charges** appear to play an important role in predicting churn behavior.\n",
        "\n",
        "Overall, the baseline model demonstrates that machine learning techniques can effectively identify customers who may be at risk of leaving the service."
