      "source": [
        "# Create a new copy of the cleaned dataset for feature engineering\n",
        "df_fe = df.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert target variable to numeric\n",
        "df_fe[\"Churn\"] = df_fe[\"Churn\"].map({\"No\": 0, \"Yes\": 1})\n",
        "\n",
        "# Feature 1: Average charges per month of tenure\n",
        "# This helps show how much a customer has paid relative to how long they have stayed.\n",
        "df_fe[\"AvgChargesPerTenure\"] = df_fe[\"TotalCharges\"] / (df_fe[\"tenure\"] + 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Feature 2: New customer flag\n",
        "# Customers with short tenure may have a higher risk of churn.\n",
        "df_fe[\"NewCustomer\"] = np.where(df_fe[\"tenure\"] <= 12, 1, 0)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Feature 3: High monthly charges flag\n",
        "# Customers paying above the median monthly charge may be more price sensitive.\n",
        "median_monthly_charge = df_fe[\"MonthlyCharges\"].median()\n",
        "df_fe[\"HighMonthlyCharges\"] = np.where(df_fe[\"MonthlyCharges\"] > median_monthly_charge, 1, 0)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Feature 4: Month-to-month contract flag\n",
        "# Month-to-month customers are often more likely to churn because they have fewer switching barriers.\n",
        "df_fe[\"MonthToMonthContract\"] = np.where(df_fe[\"Contract\"] == \"Month-to-month\", 1, 0)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Feature 5: Service count\n",
        "# This counts how many optional services each customer subscribes to.\n",
        "service_columns = [\n",
        "    \"PhoneService\",\n",
        "    \"MultipleLines\",\n",
        "    \"OnlineSecurity\",\n",
        "    \"OnlineBackup\",\n",
        "    \"DeviceProtection\",\n",
        "    \"TechSupport\",\n",
        "    \"StreamingTV\",\n",
        "    \"StreamingMovies\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "df_fe[\"ServiceCount\"] = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "for col in service_columns:\n",
        "    df_fe[\"ServiceCount\"] += np.where(df_fe[col] == \"Yes\", 1, 0)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display the new engineered features\n",
        "df_fe[\n",
        "    [\n",
        "        \"tenure\",\n",
        "        \"MonthlyCharges\",\n",
        "        \"TotalCharges\",\n",
        "        \"AvgChargesPerTenure\",\n",
        "        \"NewCustomer\",\n",
        "        \"HighMonthlyCharges\",\n",
        "        \"MonthToMonthContract\",\n",
        "        \"ServiceCount\",\n",
        "        \"Churn\"\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "].head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7v4s2Or8kZFo"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Feature Engineering Summary\n",
        "\n",
        "Several new features were created to improve the model’s ability to identify churn risk.\n",
        "\n",
        "The **AvgChargesPerTenure** feature captures how much a customer pays relative to how long they have stayed with the company. This may help identify customers who are paying a high amount but have not built long-term loyalty.\n",
        "\n",
        "The **NewCustomer** feature identifies customers with tenure of 12 months or less. This is important because the earlier analysis showed that churn is more common among customers with shorter tenure.\n",
        "\n",
        "The **HighMonthlyCharges** feature identifies customers paying above the median monthly charge. Since churned customers appeared to have higher monthly charges during EDA, this feature may help the model capture price sensitivity.\n",
        "\n",
        "The **MonthToMonthContract** feature directly flags customers with flexible contract terms. This is expected to be an important churn driver because month-to-month customers can leave more easily than customers with longer contracts.\n",
        "\n",
        "The **ServiceCount** feature measures how many services a customer uses. This may help determine whether customers with more bundled services are more or less likely to churn."
      ]
    },
