      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "k3IJ7tqYv34e"
      },
      "source": [
        "The Gradient Boosting model is trained using the same feature engineered training and testing data. Unlike logistic regression, Gradient Boosting does not require scaled features because it is based on decision trees.\n",
        "\n",
        "The model uses 200 estimators, a learning rate of 0.05, and a maximum tree depth of 3. These settings provide a balanced starting point that allows the model to learn patterns without becoming too complex."
      ]
