    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MytMSquMxLAO"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Gradient Boosting Results\n",
        "\n",
        "The Gradient Boosting model produced the strongest overall performance so far, with an accuracy score of 0.80 and a ROC-AUC score of approximately 0.840.\n",
        "\n",
        "For the non-churn class, the model performed well, with precision of 0.84, recall of 0.89, and F1-score of 0.87. This shows that the model is strong at identifying customers who are likely to stay.\n",
        "\n",
        "For the churn class, the model achieved precision of 0.64, recall of 0.53, and F1-score of 0.58. This means that when the model predicts churn, it is correct about 64% of the time. However, the recall of 0.53 shows that the model still misses some actual churned customers.\n",
        "\n",
        "The confusion matrix shows that the model correctly predicted 921 non-churn customers and 199 churn customers. It incorrectly classified 112 non-churn customers as churn and missed 175 actual churn customers.\n",
        "\n",
        "Compared to Random Forest, Gradient Boosting performed better across the main evaluation metrics. It had higher accuracy, higher churn precision, higher churn recall, higher churn F1-score, and a higher ROC-AUC score.\n",
        "\n",
        "Compared to Logistic Regression with engineered features, Gradient Boosting performed slightly better overall. The ROC-AUC increased from approximately 0.837 to 0.840, and the model identified one additional churn customer correctly.\n",
        "\n",
        "The feature importance results show that the most important predictor was MonthToMonthContract, followed by tenure, InternetService_Fiber optic, TotalCharges, MonthlyCharges, and PaymentMethod_Electronic check. This confirms that contract flexibility, customer tenure, internet service type, billing behavior, and payment method are key drivers of churn.\n",
        "\n",
        "Overall, Gradient Boosting is the strongest model tested so far. While the improvement over logistic regression is modest, it provides the best overall predictive performance and useful insight into churn drivers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7Q_whTLJxeWL"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 12. Model Comparison and Final Model Selection\n",
        "\n",
        "After training multiple models, the next step is to compare their performance side by side. This allows us to determine which model provides the best balance of accuracy, churn detection, and overall predictive strength.\n",
        "\n",
        "For this churn prediction project, ROC-AUC and churn recall are especially important. ROC-AUC measures how well the model separates churned customers from non-churned customers across different thresholds. Churn recall measures how many actual churned customers the model successfully identifies.\n",
        "\n",
        "Because the business goal is to identify customers at risk of leaving, a model that misses fewer churned customers is more useful for retention planning."
      ]
    },
