      },
      "source": [
        "### Hyperparameter Tuning Results\n",
        "\n",
        "Hyperparameter tuning was performed on the Gradient Boosting model using GridSearchCV with five-fold cross-validation and ROC-AUC as the scoring metric.\n",
        "\n",
        "The best parameters identified were:\n",
        "\n",
        "- learning_rate: 0.05\n",
        "- max_depth: 2\n",
        "- min_samples_leaf: 5\n",
        "- n_estimators: 200\n",
        "\n",
        "The best cross-validation ROC-AUC score was approximately 0.8480. This suggests that the tuned model performed well during cross-validation on the training data.\n",
        "\n",
        "When evaluated on the test set, the tuned Gradient Boosting model produced an accuracy score of approximately 0.7974 and a ROC-AUC score of approximately 0.8397.\n",
        "\n",
        "For the churn class, the tuned model achieved precision of 0.65, recall of 0.52, and F1-score of 0.58. The confusion matrix showed that the model correctly predicted 927 non-churn customers and 195 churn customers. However, it missed 179 actual churn customers.\n",
        "\n",
        "Compared to the original Gradient Boosting model, the tuned model slightly improved accuracy and churn precision, but it slightly reduced churn recall and ROC-AUC. Since the business goal is to identify customers who are likely to churn, recall and ROC-AUC are especially important.\n",
        "\n",
        "For that reason, the original Gradient Boosting model remains the preferred final model. It had a slightly higher ROC-AUC score and identified more actual churn customers than the tuned version."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
