        "id": "I0OiNcog2k4E"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 14. Model Interpretation With SHAP\n",
        "\n",
        "After selecting the original Gradient Boosting model as the final model, the next step is to interpret the model using SHAP values.\n",
        "\n",
        "SHAP values help explain how each feature contributes to the model’s predictions. This is useful because it allows us to understand which variables increase or decrease churn risk.\n",
        "\n",
        "For this project, SHAP helps connect the machine learning results back to business insights. Instead of only reporting model accuracy, we can identify the customer characteristics that most strongly influence churn predictions."
      ]
    },
