        "id": "MK_CJc-I5YUD"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 16. Threshold Analysis for Final Model\n",
        "\n",
        "The original Gradient Boosting model was selected as the final model because it achieved the strongest overall ROC-AUC and the best churn recall among the models tested.\n",
        "\n",
        "However, the default classification threshold of 0.50 may not be optimal for a churn prediction problem. In customer churn, false negatives are especially important because they represent customers who actually churned but were not identified by the model.\n",
        "\n",
        "To better align the model with the business objective of identifying high-risk customers, multiple probability thresholds are evaluated. Lowering the threshold may increase churn recall by identifying more at-risk customers, but it may also increase false positives."
      ]
    },
